## 📌 Project Overview

This project demonstrates the design and deployment of a **highly available static web application infrastructure on AWS using Terraform**.

The application is hosted on **Amazon EC2 instances running in private subnets across multiple Availability Zones**. An **Application Load Balancer (ALB)** distributes incoming HTTP traffic between healthy EC2 instances.

An **Auto Scaling Group (ASG)** maintains the required number of web servers and automatically launches replacement instances when required.

The complete AWS infrastructure is provisioned using **Terraform Infrastructure as Code (IaC)**.

The web application is served using **Nginx**, with automated deployment through EC2 `user_data`.

---

# 🏗️ Architecture

The infrastructure consists of:

- Custom AWS VPC
- Public and private subnets
- Multiple Availability Zones
- Internet Gateway
- NAT Gateway
- Application Load Balancer
- Target Group
- Auto Scaling Group
- Private EC2 instances
- Nginx web server
- IAM role for AWS Systems Manager
- Terraform Infrastructure as Code

### Architecture Diagram

![AWS Architecture](screenshots/architecture.png)

---

# 🌐 Application

A static website template from **Tooplate – Orbital** is deployed on the EC2 web servers.

The EC2 Launch Template automatically:

1. Installs Nginx
2. Installs required packages
3. Downloads the website template
4. Extracts the template
5. Copies the website files to the Nginx document root
6. Configures permissions
7. Starts Nginx

The application is accessed through the **Application Load Balancer DNS endpoint**.

